String-search investigation (operator priority: strchr, strnlen,
strncmp, memchr). No recipe changes; no patch wired.

BASELINE (live libc, Egg): strchr found 1.6-5.6ns (SWAR strchrnul,
already fast); strnlen bounded SWAR; strncmp eq 6.1/28.6/100.9/1504ns
for 16/64/256/4K (byte loop ~0.37ns/B); memcmp eq 3.5/19.4/758ns
(byte loop); memchr SWAR ~0.04ns/B long scans. Compiler does NOT
auto-vectorize any of these (verified: zero SIMD/rep in built
objects) — early-exit search idioms defeat the vectorizer.

SKETCHES (SSE2, page-guarded 16B blocks; strncmp NUL-aware both
sides): differential vs live libc 120,000 checks x 5 hosts
(Egg/route/keeper/minimer/homer, musl AND glibc) = 600,000 total,
0 FAILS. Guard-page child-isolated runs included. One harness bug
found and fixed during the work (low-canary overlap on forward
deltas flagged both impls identically — same lesson as memmove).

RESULTS (sketch vs current, min/5):
strncmp eq: Egg 4.4/8.6/9.1/8.3x (16/64/256/4K); route 4.7-7.9x;
keeper 5.0-8.5x; minimer 3.9-7.6x; homer 4.4-9.1x.
memcmp eq: 5.5-8.7x (64B), 6.0-7.0x (4K) across hosts.
memchr absent: 1.6-2.6x (64B/4K/64K) across hosts.

VERDICTS:
PROPOSE strncmp + memcmp arch work (6-9x sustained, all hosts,
short-string behaviour preserved: eq16 still wins 4-5x).
HOLD memchr/strchr/strnlen (1.6-2.6x long-only; SWAR C already
decent; page-guard complexity in the hot loop not justified).
strcmp shares the strncmp shape but was NOT measured — not proposed.
Translation sketch->arch .s is mechanical on implementation GO;
evidence bar for wiring: re-run matrix vs built libc + static-PIE
+ testsuite, same as rint/memmove.

Rule kept throughout: measure first (sqrt/FMA precedent); page-safe
loads only (in-page check); no new ISA (SSE2 baseline); no ABI or
observable-contract change.
